{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sensor noise sensor noise","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","fileName":"Sensor Noise.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sensor Noise","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sensor noise sensor noise","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","fileName":"Sensor Noise.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sensor Noise","heading":"Sensor Noise","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Sensor noise is the variation added when a camera converts light into digital measurements. It includes changing random components as well as stable differences in how individual sensor elements respond to the same illumination.\n\nForensic analysis uses both properties. Random-noise level should vary plausibly with brightness and camera processing, while the stable component can identify a device. Denoising, sharpening, compression, resizing, saturation, and low exposure all alter the observable signal.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sensor noise sensor noise","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Noise.md","fileName":"Sensor Noise.md","folder":"6 - Full Not